        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lower Manhattan, Manhattan, New York City, United States\n- Buildings: One Liberty Plaza, U.S. Steel Building, Singer Building, City Investing Building, 1717 Broadway\n- Topics: skyscrapers, hotel height records\n\nFacts:\n- One Liberty Plaza, formerly the U.S. Steel Building, is a skyscraper in Lower Manhattan in New York City.\n- One Liberty Plaza stands at the site of the former Singer Building and the former City Investing Building.\n- The Singer Building was the tallest structure ever dismantled.\n- 1717 Broadway is a skyscraper in Manhattan, New York City, United States.\n- 1717 Broadway is 750 feet tall.\n- 1717 Broadway is the tallest hotel in North America.",
